@page "/"

<PageTitle>Textbook Chapter Question Generator</PageTitle>

<div class="container-fluid mt-4">
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12 text-center">
            <h2 class="display-5">Textbook Chapter Question Generator</h2>
            <p class="text-muted">
                Paste a textbook chapter and configure question types and Bloom's Taxonomy levels.
                The pipeline analyses the content and generates MCQs, short-answer questions, essay prompts,
                and true/false statements — all in parallel.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-12">
            <QuestionGeneratorWidget />
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row mt-5">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="alert alert-info" role="alert">
                <h5 class="alert-heading">
                    <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-2"></i>How It Works
                </h5>
                <p class="mb-0">
                    The pipeline runs three stages:
                    <strong>content analysis</strong> — the chapter is analysed by an LLM to extract key
                    concepts and map them to Bloom's Taxonomy levels;
                    <strong>parallel generation</strong> — <code>Task.WhenAll</code> fans out four LLM calls
                    simultaneously, generating MCQs (with distractors), short-answer questions (with model answers
                    and marking criteria), essay prompts (with rubrics), and true/false statements (with
                    justifications) — all calibrated to your selected Bloom's levels;
                    <strong>assembly</strong> — all question types are merged into a unified question bank with
                    summary counts per type and per Bloom's level.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
